      "title": "Resolving Config Manager Query Timeouts from Resource Exhaustion",
      "content_summary": "Addresses query timeouts in Config Manager caused by resource exhaustion, manifesting as high replication lag, index corruption, and slow response times.",
      "content_body": "When Config Manager queries time out alongside high replication lag and index corruption, the root cause is typically resource exhaustion or capacity limitations. First, check the infrastructure metrics for CPU and memory saturation on the database hosts. If the system is at its capacity limit, a simple rate limit adjustment may provide temporary relief, but a capacity increase is usually required. In severe cases where hardware cannot be scaled effectively, infrastructure replacement may be necessary to restore performance."
